<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sakhalin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sakhalin is a large island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-far-east">Russian Far East</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hokkaido">Hokkaido</a>. Its original inhabitants included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ainu">Ainu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nivkh-people">Nivkh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orok-people">Orok peoples</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> shared it from 1855 until 1875, when Russia took the whole island. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-portsmouth">Treaty of Portsmouth</a> of 1905 gave Japan the south as Karafuto, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> occupied in 1945, and the island is now Russia's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakhalin-oblast">Sakhalin Oblast</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sakhalin.jpg" alt="Sakhalin" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: edited by M.Minderhoud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sakhalin_(detail).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
